  "answer": "This has been requested before. PowerToys#38665 asks for the same thing for the Command Palette's System Commands: being able to use English names (as PowerToys Run allowed) when the system locale is non-English. It was closed as a duplicate of #38593, which is the thread tracking it, so follow that one and add your Japanese IME scenario there. PowerToys#46304 is the broader request to search in both English and the display language. A maintainer replied that partial support exists for Pinyin, and that how far to take it and how to expose it in the API is still open. No fix or workaround is documented in these tickets yet. Until one ships, you have to type the localized name (e.g. 再起動). Windows Terminal added combined English and display-language search in 1.24, which shows the approach is feasible."
